OpenMW-DS: background threads on the little cores, the Lua worker on the big ones.

On Android the scheduler places threads by load, not priority. The idle priority navmesh
thread took a big core while building tiles, and the Lua worker, idle most of each frame, was
put on a little core; a frame with more Lua work then ran there at half speed and the main
thread waited for it (frames of 40-55 ms while walking).

